-- The name `presumed` gives a default taken at a named site is the rule's (or
-- record's) own name as its declaration writes it, whatever the site called it
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md T6b, review m1, 2026-10-03). Three things used
-- to leak into it: an AKA alias, the section a rule is declared in, and a mixfix
-- rule's canonical pattern. `scaled` is called by its own name, by its alias and
-- by its section-qualified name; the answer lists it once, as `scaled`.

§ `Pricing`

DECLARE Config
  HAS timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 30
      retries IS A NUMBER

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled AKA rescaled MEANS rate TIMES base

GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      factor IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2
GIVETH A NUMBER
base `scaled by` factor MEANS base TIMES factor

§ `Use`

@export default Combine
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS
  (scaled WITH base IS n)
    PLUS (rescaled WITH base IS n)
    PLUS (`Pricing`.scaled WITH base IS n)
    PLUS (`scaled by` WITH base IS n)
    PLUS (Config WITH retries IS n)'s timeout
